    "updated_at": "2016-04-26T21:23:26Z",
    "body": "Re, support: slightly dated but [mostly accurate overview](http://chimera.labs.oreilly.com/books/1230000000545/ch10.html#SPECULATIVE_HINTS). \n- Ignore \"subresource\", we've deprecated that in favor of rel=preload.\n- Given that we have at least two implementations for each one, I'd say all of them qualify.\n\nWhen you say \"add them to HTML\", do you mean: \n- Add them to the https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#linkTypes table\n- For each one, add a section linking to RH definition? I'd love to avoid duplication.\n\nSpeaking of which, my proposal would be simplify prefetch definition within the HTML spec itself and link it to the RH definition.. same as we would do for prerender, dns-prefetch, preconnect. Does that sound reasonable?\n",
