    "created_at": "2016-04-27T21:54:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-27T21:54:40Z",
    "body": "> Given that we have at least two implementations for each one, I'd say all of them qualify.\n\nGreat!\n\n> When you say \"add them to HTML\", do you mean: \n\nYes, both those things. In addition, HTML would define things like adding the link rels to `<a>`, `<area>`, and `<link>`s supported tokens lists, or whether the link types are body-ok, since HTML currently does that for all the other link types. But it would defer all the processing model to RH, with maybe a short summary sentence.\n\n> Speaking of which, my proposal would be simplify prefetch definition within the HTML spec itself and link it to the RH definition.. same as we would do for prerender, dns-prefetch, preconnect. Does that sound reasonable?\n\nDefinitely; that's exactly what I was thinking.\n",
